# Categories authored by this server. See `.local/content.sym` for why these live
# in `.local/` rather than the upstream symbol files.
#
# Id allocation: vanilla categories occupy 1..1915 and grow upward; RSMod's own
# three occupy 65532..65534 and grow *downward*. Ours start at 50000 in the middle
# of that gap, so neither side can reach us. Duplicate ids are only detected within
# a single file, so staying out of both bands is what keeps a future upstream
# category from silently aliasing one of ours.
#
# These two extend `params.npc_attack_type` past the three melee types. OSRS's own
# npc `attacktype` field has exactly this five-value domain; upstream only ever
# authored the melee three because `NvPCombat` was melee-only and nothing could
# have read the other two.
50000	attacktype_ranged
50001	attacktype_magic
